.TH XZILE 1 "2026" "XZile 2.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xzile \- XZile eXtends Zile, a lightweight Emacs clone
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xzile
[\fIOPTION-OR-FILENAME\fR]...
.br
.B xzile-gui
[\fIOPTION-OR-FILENAME\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
XZile is a lightweight Emacs clone that provides a subset of Emacs's
functionality suitable for basic editing.
.PP
.B xzile-gui
is the same editor in a window of its own, with the system clipboard,
mouse support, and the variables \fBgui-font\fR and
\fBgui-font-size\fR to choose its font.
If built with image and PDF support, it shows image and PDF files as
previews that cannot be saved (\fBimage-mode\fR, \fBpdf-mode\fR;
\fBpreview-binary-files\fR turns this off).
In \fBhtml-mode\fR, \fBhtml-preview\fR (C-c C-v) shows the file in a
browser engine window:
.B xzile-html-preview
on Linux, or the default browser.
.PP
In the file picker of \fBfind-file\fR (C-x C-f) and \fBdired\fR (C-x d),
M-l chooses a location: this machine, or another reached with
.BR ssh (1)
(an alias from \fI~/.ssh/config\fR, a recent or saved connection, or
a new host, user and port); the prompt names it.
Remote text files can be visited, created, saved and reverted, and
remote directories browsed in Dired; commands that would change files
from Dired or run programs are refused in remote buffers.
ssh runs with BatchMode=yes, so keys or an agent are needed and host
keys are checked; \fBremote-timeout\fR bounds each operation, C-g
cancels it, and \fBssh-config-file\fR chooses the ssh configuration.
.SS "Initialization options:"
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-init\-file\fR, \fB\-q\fR
do not load ~/.xzile
.TP
\fB\-\-funcall\fR, \fB\-f\fR FUNC
call XZile Lisp function FUNC with no arguments
.TP
\fB\-\-load\fR, \fB\-l\fR FILE
load XZile Lisp FILE using the load function
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\-log\fR FILE
append debug logs to FILE
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\-categories\fR CATS
comma-separated debug categories, e.g. syntax,filetype
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
display this help message and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
display version information and exit
.SS "Action options:"
.TP
FILE
visit FILE using find-file
.TP
+LINE FILE
visit FILE using find-file, then go to line LINE
.PP
Exit status is 0 if OK, 1 if it cannot start up, for example because
of an invalid command-line argument, and 2 if it crashes or runs out
of memory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERM
Used to decide whether the terminal supports colours.
.TP
.BR LINES ", " COLUMNS
If set, override the size of the terminal.
.TP
.BR XZILE_DEBUG ", " XZILE_DEBUG_LOG
Debug categories and log file, as for the debug options.
.SH FILES
~/.xzile \(em user's XZile init file
.PP
/usr/local/share/doc/xzile/dotzile.sample \(em which contains some useful
code for the init file.
.PP
~/.ssh/config \(em ssh configuration, whose Host aliases are offered as
remote locations.
.PP
~/.xzile.d/locations \(em connections that worked, and the directory
last browsed on each machine; private, replaced atomically under an
fcntl lock on ~/.xzile.d/locations.lock, and not used with \fB\-q\fR.
See README.md for its format.
